cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: Cerulion
abstract: >-
  Cerulion gives AI agents a harness to control real robots. This repository
  holds the open-source runtime: a zero-copy robot runtime that records runs to
  MCAP and re-runs supported native recordings against new code, rmw_cerulion
  for ROS 2 (validated on Jazzy), and cerulion-rcpd, an MCP server through
  which an agent calls only the tools the robot's operator declares
  (not in the 1.0.0 release).
# Founders as personal authors (citation credit), then the entity;
# further individual contributors are credited in docs/legal/AUTHORS.
authors:
  - family-names: Sharma
    given-names: Lakshay
  - family-names: Kariyawasam
    given-names: Raveen
  - name: "Cerulion Inc. and contributors"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-21"
url: "https://github.com/cerulion-inc/cerulion"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cerulion-inc/cerulion"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - robotics
  - ai-agents
  - mcp
  - zero-copy
  - ROS2
  - iceoryx2
  - real-time
  - pub-sub
